  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of the insufficient gross internal area for Flat 1, poor internal vertical stacking arrangements, and the location of a ground floor bedroom beside a refuse store would result in a substandard form of accommodation that would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. In addition to this, the poor quality of accommodation proposed means that a satisfactory compensatory 3+ bedroom unit has not been provided, the proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP4 and CP5 of the Enfield Plan Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5 and DMD9 of the Development Management Document (2014), the Technical Housing Standards Nationally Described Space Standard (2015) and the Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).",
    "The proposed layout of the forecourt, by reason of the number of structures required and proposed to be sited within it, would result in a cluttered and cramped frontage that would cause visual harm to the street scene, and fail to provide a comfortable or a well-designed access route, the proposed development would therefore fail to meet the high-quality design aspirations of National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3, D5 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP25 of the Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD6 and DMD45 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed rear terrace, by reason of the detailed design and materials would be discordant within the terrace and surrounding area. The proposal would have an adverse visual impact on the character and appearance of the host property and the wider terrace, contrary to London Plan (2021) Policy D4, Core Strategy Policy CP30 (2010) and Development Management Document (2014) Policy DMD37."
  ],
